    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d352">

                <pb facs="0577" n="559" sameAs="frus:frus1948v03/pg559"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860S.5151/3–548: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        United States Political Adviser</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Joyce</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">at
                        Trieste</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-03-09T18:00:00-05:00">March 9, 1948—6 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>96. Urtel 108 March 5.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d352-f1"/> Confirm Deptel same
                    date 91.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d352-f2"/> Proposed $20 million program covers
                    chiefly items now supplied PL 84. Tentative
                    breakdown 15–month program follows (all figures in long tons):</p>
                <p>Wheat 62.180, edible fats (lard) 3.820, horsemeat 810, milk, evaporated 5,090,
                    pulses 5,100, coal 240,000 and industrial fats 900. Also $315 thousand for
                    medical supplies and $200 thousand for fibers incentive and other goods.</p>
                <p>Sent to Rome.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d352-f1" n="1" xml:id="d352-f1-content">
                <p>In this telegram, not printed, Joyce referred to a report that Secretary Marshall
                    requested Congress for $20 million for Trieste through the fiscal year 1949. He
                    asked about the specific purpose of this sum: to combat disease and unrest, or
                    to foster economic rehabilitation. (860S.5151/3–548)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d352-f2" n="2" xml:id="d352-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
